**[[00:17](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D17)]** Let's discuss the second commandment according to the oldest, that is, the Jewish enumeration of the Ten Commandments. In Christian tradition, it's the first commandment.

**[[00:24](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D24)]** Well, we're doing it again, ladles and gentle sporks: part two of the Ten Commandments! And the big, dumb, already old mate Dennis has to make it all so fuzzy and confusing. The second commandment is also the first? You would think the God man would have gotten that straight for you at least.

**[[00:45](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D45)]** And now, does that mean they're in a different order, or is the one that was first now gone, perhaps later replaced with a better commandment—like, I don't know, "Don't do slavery"? 'Cause I know last time you tried to pretend God hates that, but accidentally forgot that the very next part of the book he talks about how to do slavery properly. Oopsy daisy!

**[[01:02](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D62)]** Anyway, enough preamble, let's get on with this shizz.

**[[01:12](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D72)]** The most common translation begins: *"You shall have no other gods before me."*

**[[01:16](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D76)]** Okay, already some questions pop to mind. First, about your wording: "most common translations." Okay, but you know that doesn't mean that they're right, right? Just because it's common doesn't mean it's not a screw-up, just popular! And second, "no gods before me"—ah, so there ARE other gods? Good to know! And I can have them, just not BEFORE I have you? I guess Yahweh just isn't into sloppy seconds.

**[[01:42](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D102)]** Sorry, I had to do that because of the law of sex jokes. But seriously, can we have other gods or no? And are there other gods or no? You would think that a better commandment might be: *"I am the only God, the rest are made-up bullshit, and even if they weren't, don't worship any of those assholes—they are so mean, didn't even come to my birthday party just because I said they don't exist."* Sad God face!

**[[02:09](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D129)]** The commandment then goes on to prohibit both making idols and worshiping idols. Most people, when they think of this commandment, understandably think that it only prohibits the worship of idols and the worship of gods such as the ancient pagan gods of rain, of fertility, all the other nature gods, and chief gods such as the Roman Jupiter and the Greek Zeus.

**[[02:30](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D150)]** What a bunch of idiots! They expected that the thing that God said was what he actually meant! Why would he do that? Why, oh why, would the most competent being in the universe be capable of explicitly stating his exact desires and using the words he needs to state them clearly? No, no, no, that's not how literally every rule of communication works all of the time! You have to say one thing but mean something else entirely, and never, ever, ever say the thing you really wanted!

**[[02:59](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D179)]** Now, that does mean you do end up with the teeny-tiny, itty-bitty, microscopic problem of: if everything you say is up for interpretation, then no one is ever going to be able to know what you actually mean! But that seems like a small price to pay for what is clearly perfect clarity, right?

**[[03:17](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D197)]** However, there is a major problem with this understanding of the commandment: since no one today worships these gods, let alone worships idols made of stone, most people think that this commandment is irrelevant to modern life.

**[[03:33](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D213)]** You know, that would be a really good point if it wasn't completely wrong! There are still plenty of religions that arguably have idols and the like, what are you talking about, you ignorant goon? But okay, let's just say that they didn't. Well, then it's almost like it was written in a different time by people with no ability to understand that the world could or would change, so they assumed people would always have various other kinds of religions in that particular vein, so they stuck to what they understood with no additional fluff.

**[[04:07](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D247)]** Because, of course, if they were in fact getting them from some sort of omnipotent deity, it might, you know, have said something like: *"Oh, and don't forget, when there are no more graven images and idols and all that shit, swap this rule out for something like: 'Thou shalt not rev thy engine at a stop sign in a quiet neighborhood.'"* Don't worry, they'll understand that in a few thousand years.

**[[04:32](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D272)]** The irony, however, is that this commandment is not only relevant to modern life, it is in many ways the mother of all the other commandments.

**[[04:38](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D278)]** Dennis, you hyped up the last one just as much, and it was a silly thing to do then! Not only because none of the rest work without this one, making them all failures on their own, but if you try to do it for all of them, it's really going to start becoming obvious that that's what you're doing. Also, I don't know how this is going to be the "mother" of things like "don't kill" or "don't steal" or any of the other ones, really. I mean, when I kill and steal, it's not because I'm doing it for some kind of god! And if you tell anyone otherwise, may Cyist take you and may the Grave Fox take all your stuff to boot!

**[[05:12](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D312)]** Why is it so relevant today? Because today we have as many false gods as the ancients did.

**[[05:18](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D318)]** It's so lame! The whole "everyone worships X, Y, Z today" thing is so dumb. Like, seriously, 'cause it's always conflating someone liking something with ongoing and active worship and sacrifice! But comparing religious worship to most things—like even trees, and... is that supposed to be the Oscars? I don't think anyone even cares about the Oscars, let alone worships the damn thing! But even like money—sure, people do get an unhealthy obsession with the acquisition of wealth, but that's not the same thing as worship! It's more of an addiction than anything, and addictions are not the same as worship. I mean, unless you really want to invite an incredibly unflattering comparison to yourselves, I wouldn't go there—mostly because it would force me to sing: *"Might as well face it, you're addicted to God!"* And no one wants that, I'll end up surrounded by guitar-playing Liliths from *Cheers*.

**[[06:21](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D381)]** And why is it the mother of all the other commandments? Because if we identify false gods and avoid worshiping them, we will eliminate one of the greatest barriers to a good world: false gods.

**[[06:36](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D396)]** But what? How does that work? This is the mother of all commandments because it's about the thing it says it's about, and also about an interpretation of the thing that it's about that covers some other thing that largely has nothing to do with all the other commandments? Dennis, I'm sure this sounded smart as it echoed around your empty skull, but that's not anything! That's saying something is something because it's not that! Still to this day baffles me that there are people who think that Dennis is a good speaker with smart ideas.

**[[07:07](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D427)]** So let's begin by defining a false god: Dennis Prager. No, seriously, if you are going to play the "everything people pretty much pay attention to is worship," well, oh boy! Not only would that apply to DP and his PU, but also you can sacrifice to them on top! I mean, what are donations if not a sacrifice of some amount of your needs?

**[[07:27](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D447)]** Speaking of, if you want to donate some of your hard-earned to a truly worthy cause, you can always join my Patreon or memberships, and you will know that a portion of that money will go to support the emptying of vast sums of whiskey directly into my face! A noble effort to stop other people from having to drink that terrible, terrible, delicious stuff. I've said it before, but I am basically Drunk Super Jesus, and we already know that he was a pisshead!

**[[07:54](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D474)]** The point of biblical monotheism is that there is only one God, and that only this God—the creator of the universe who demands that we keep these Ten Commandments—is to be worshiped.

**[[08:08](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D488)]** I mean, no wonder you think that this one was the mother of all the others! I don't think Dennis knows what a definition is. But to be fair, us idiots thought that when he said he was going to define a false god, he was actually going to do that instead of talking about fucking monotheism! You know what? My bad. That's what I get for not having low enough expectations from Dennis. They were on the floor when they clearly should have been several miles under it!

**[[08:35](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D515)]** Why? First, because one God means one human race. Only if we all have the same creator or father, as it were, are we all brothers and sisters.

**[[08:48](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D528)]** Still not a definition of a false god! How does that work? I mean, in most polytheistic religions, if humans come from those gods, they're still a part of humanity! Also, the fact is, human beings are absolutely part of the same species even without any kind of god! But worst of all, that "one God" allegedly making us all brothers has historically caused more than his fair share of ripping friends, families, and even nations apart—because he, again, failed to make a clear expression of what he actually wanted! So a bunch of different groups formed, all equally certain they knew what he wanted, and equally willing to kill everybody that didn't agree with them about it. And that's not to mention if you did follow a "wrong" god instead of being lucky enough to be born into the right place and time to already believe in the correct one, and more than likely believed that HE was the very definition of a false god—which, A, at least I've given one, and B, is kind of true. I mean, they're all false gods, but that's only because they don't real.

**[[09:51](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D591)]** Second, having the same parent also means that no person or group is intrinsically more valuable than any other...

**[[09:58](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D598)]** ...as long as they, again, had the good fortune to be born into the right time and place to the correct family, and didn't have too much of a brain to question the obvious stupidity of God-man's Bible club! Otherwise, they are less than scum of the earth who deserve to be put to the sword and/or eternal torture. Hey man, it's your book though, don't blame me! And that's the thing: you can say these 10 random commands or statements or assortment of words mean anything, but the behavior of God and his people in his book suggests some pretty specific interpretations that are not "love everybody a whole huggy bunch," that's for damn sure!

