**[[12:51](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D771)]** But like, WHO the hell actually worships those things the same way one would worship a religious being, with fervor and what have you? Again, it's just not the same! And while I can guess where he's going with the education thing, it's doubly dumbly with art and love. Like, who the hell worships any art that isn't intrinsically related to some religious shit? And brings up another question of why that shit exists: "Oh, it makes you feel the grandeur of God!" I mean, maybe, but it's still the art giving you those feelings, not the actual God! Just sounds like more idolatry, man!

**[[13:24](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D804)]** Yes, any of these often wonderful things, when worshiped, can lead to terrible results. Take art: many of the cruelest humans in history loved beautiful music and art. But as a music lover, I learned early in life the sad fact that great music can be used to inspire people to follow evil just as much as it can be used to inspire people to do good.

**[[13:55](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D835)]** No, no, no, no! Character break, Sir Sic mode off! I can't even begin to explain how that is probably by far the stupidest thing I have heard in my entire life! Are you actually kidding me, Dennis? I'm sorry, but what atrocities were committed as a direct result of someone liking a piece of freaking music? And it has to be something, mind, that the person would never, ever have done without liking some random ditty! Even when people say "Marilyn Manson made me do it," that's just a bullshit excuse for being a massive piece of garbage! And this becomes especially confounding when, again, the fact that many, many, many of the worst acts in human history were committed as a direct result of people worshiping YOUR specific God—many of them written down as good things in your various books! I mean, seriously, I can only assume that this was supposed to be "bad people like music too," but bad people like everything everyone likes! Being a miserable bastard isn't a prerequisite to being evil, but if he had said that, I know it would have been even more obvious what a staggeringly absurd thing to say it was. Goddamn it!

