**[[17:37](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D1057)]** Okay, so what? I'm sure that, again, education isn't what caused either of those things! Again, it's a tool, a thing that people can have. You know, you could have made some kind of point that when a bad person is also highly educated, that makes them more dangerous than they otherwise might be, but again, the education itself would have had little to do with the specific choices they make. And do you really want to play the game with Nazi Germany? I mean, they wouldn't have all been extremely highly educated, but you know what? 95% of the population was Christian, God-fearing frickwits who thought that the God of the Bible was totally on their side! And I would bet that there are more than a few passages they thought completely justified that shit! Not a great look, not going to lie.

