**[[19:29](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D1169)]** Oh, now you could just piss right off into space! That's not even remotely the same kind of love that anyone in the freaking universe would ever be talking about, and you know it! Yeah, sure, being overly attached to a piece of freaking ground is going to make someone do stupid and probably bad things, because it's dumb, everybody knows that! But don't forget, a lot of people associate God and country as the same thing to them, don't pretend otherwise, matey!

**[[19:56](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DjGcxApVFa2c%26t%3D1196)]** And here's a test for you: imagine that the pet you love and a stranger—a person you don't know and therefore could not possibly love—are drowning. Do you first try to save your pet or the stranger? Well, if love is an end in itself, you save your pet. But if you hold human life as a higher value than love, you won't follow love.

